    "narrative": "As we look at today\u2019s slate on July 16, 2026, the Austin Waves offense faces a challenging day of situational volatility. Our most reliable pivot point in the lineup is **Jackson Merrill**, who anchors our offensive potential despite a neutral matchup. His efficiency score remains the ceiling for the squad today, as his ability to consistently put the ball in play provides the highest floor for our AVG category, which remains a focal point as we hunt for efficiency over sheer volume. Conversely, we are keeping a close watch on **Jorge Polanco**, who slots in at a marginal 50.85; while he is currently active, the 31% rain risk in his matchup against Nola, A presents a tangible threat to his ability to complete a full day of plate appearances. Should the skies open, we are prepared to shift reliance toward **Heliot Ramos**, whose recent power metrics against RHP give us a high-upside alternative if the weather forecast deteriorates further.\n\nThe bench remains heavy with talent, though the optimization process was largely dictated by the unavailability of our core anchors **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, all of whom are off today. The most difficult \"sit\" decision involved **Josh Lowe**; while his sprint speed profiles as an elite asset in our pursuit of scarce SB, his historical BvP splits against today\u2019s opposing starter pushed him just below the threshold of our preferred start, with **Jordan Westburg** taking the spot due to a superior OBP projection. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor **Luis Robert Jr.** on the IL, as his absence remains the primary drag on our weekly SB totals. Elsewhere, **Nasim Nunez** and **Sam Antonacci** are being utilized sparingly to preserve our game caps, ensuring that we have roster flexibility as we approach the weekend series. We remain particularly sensitive to the health status of **Jacob Wilson** and **Coby Mayo** as they integrate into our daily rotation; their ability to contribute to our HR totals will be vital to offsetting the lack of production from **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Brayan Rocchio** in current favorable hitting conditions.",
